test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T13:38:36.2181316Z             "body": "This private local fork preserves the original stdio MCP surface and adds bounded batch/durable-job execution. The candidate remains draft and is not release-ready.\n\nThe runtime deterministically prepares pinned Playwright/core1.64.1 with explicit VP9 BT.601 matrix metadata, using exact source/output hashes and bundled dependencies. Scripts-disabled production installs resolve the same private prepared core. No runtime interception or recording rewriting is used as a product fix. Caller-supplied contexts/remote servers retain their host encoder. See docs/DEPENDENCY_PATCHES.md for provenance, payload and upgrade review.\n\nLatest completed native86 atfd1939c: batch1566/6, original including legacy552/5, combined2118/11. All five configured main lanes ran; Windows203 vs Linux22/24 and Mac211 is explicit platform case scoping. Five297-file production checks, four132/133-test component lanes, Docker hash/two endpoint cases and all three actual Codex1k clients passed (model0/owned0). These healthy samples do not clear native85's schema timeout/unconfirmed worker exit or older identity gaps.\n\nRemaining failures: Mac SDK979/sync989 deadlines; Windows Firefox cold startup before any /429 request, pointer/locator, retry lifecycle and direct-pipe cases; Mac Chromium screenshot protocol capture; Mac WebKit248/37/0 color; Windows WebKit WAV/VP9 readiness. Upstream v1.64.1 explicitly excludes WebKit/Windows WebM/audio playback tests, but this fork retains strict failing assertions and does not claim the exact WAV mechanism. All36 new hydration/lazy/offline-worker cases passed. Independent Mac server/pipe1k and three Windows10-fresh/230-action controls passed; stock-headed control failed after5 actions/context_timeout. No default transport/channel change or cause-fix inference.\n\nAll17 logs plus an EOF first-read/partial log are archived. One new full legacy comparison retains a current birth mismatch against a captured same-PID incarnation; another root row lacks a captured birth. This is narrow evidence only: old136/142 cohorts, missing birth ledgers, unknown exits, leases/debt and other acceptance gaps remain unresolved. No name/role/age/window filtering, unsafe replay, assertion waiver or budget increase.\n\nThis follow-up adds owned upload-event witnesses (a deliberate bounded stall proves one click POST despite failed ACK), browser/phase labels for highlight captures, and a corrected video-probe gate. Successful tool replies echo source; the old substring-only condition incorrectly entered optional probes on healthy results. The corrected condition requires an actual error, with zero healthy control receipts in local tests. Explicit mode samples6 variants; an isolated original-core Firefox negative still exits1 with3 automatically sampled copies and exact dependency restoration. Copies preserve encoded-stream hashes and never replace the original pixel result. Native86 lacked stock ffmpeg, so its metadata controls were unexecuted. Optional Mac-only Homebrew setup now has a separate5m bound; setup failure remains visible while original tests continue. Existing job/test/action/RPC bounds remain unchanged.\n\nLocal follow-up validation: upload2/2 each Node20/22/24 plus actual1/expected1 negative; highlight2/2 Node24; corrected video default2/2 with0 probes, explicit2/2 with6 samples, original-core negative1 as expected; strict typecheck/generated-doc lint/actionlint and297-file pack audit pass. WebKit engine and Mac tool setup remain unexecuted locally. Earlier installed-runtime and full local92-case proofs retain exact source phases.\n\nNative87 atb279f0d:\n- [Local batch QA39778440595](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39778440595)\n- [Original CI39778440886](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39778440886)\n\nEvidence/gates: docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT.md, docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md, docs/evidence/native86-summary.json, native86-completed-archive.json and native87-local-final-proof.json. Pending outcomes are not passes. No merge or publication is proposed.\n",
